WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.041 --> 00:00:07.041
(Robert): Aerys Targaryen was the last
of his name to sit on the Iron Throne.

00:00:07.172 --> 00:00:10.507
Known far and wide as the Mad King,

00:00:10.508 --> 00:00:14.011
his was a reign of instability and terror.

00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:17.681
The Seven Kingdoms are
well rid of him and his kind.

00:00:17.682 --> 00:00:21.310
Oh, he may have appeared to be
a capable ruler at first,

00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:24.188
but that was due in no small part
to his councilors,

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:28.066
led by the Hand of the King,
Tywin Lannister.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:32.946
There may have been years of peace
and prosperity during Aerys' reign,

00:00:32.947 --> 00:00:35.824
but it was Tywin who was really
running the country,

00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:40.078
as Aerys spiraled further
and further into insanity.

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:44.416
The dragon spawn were famous
for losing their minds.

00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:49.417
It was the price they paid for centuries
of keeping the bloodlines pure.

00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:52.424
And Aerys more than happily continued

00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:57.425
the noble sister-fucking tradition
of his forefathers.

00:00:57.764 --> 00:01:02.764
As the years passed, Aerys' behavior
became increasingly erratic.

00:01:03.353 --> 00:01:06.230
He cut himself so often on his Iron Throne,

00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:09.191
many referred to him as King Scab,

00:01:09.192 --> 00:01:12.069
though never to his face.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:15.781
It was rumored he had developed
an obsession with wildfire,

00:01:15.782 --> 00:01:18.450
and was known 
to inflict horrific punishments

00:01:18.451 --> 00:01:20.619
on those he considered enemies,

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.413
including burning them alive.

00:01:23.414 --> 00:01:26.917
As his paranoia and blood-lust grew,

00:01:26.918 --> 00:01:29.795
he had a bitter falling-out with Lord Tywin

00:01:29.796 --> 00:01:34.466
who had served the Crown
faithfully for 20 years.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:39.467
At least Tywin was able to leave the job
with his life and fortunes intact.

00:01:39.847 --> 00:01:44.476
Subsequent Hands of King Aerys
weren't so fortunate.

00:01:44.477 --> 00:01:48.355
Then the Targaryens went too far.

00:01:48.356 --> 00:01:52.776
The Crown Prince Rhaegar
abducted Lyanna Stark,

00:01:52.777 --> 00:01:57.114
daughter of Rickard Stark,
the Lord of Winterfell.

00:01:57.115 --> 00:02:02.115
She was my betrothed. She was my beloved.

00:02:02.245 --> 00:02:05.205
Beautiful and spirited woman.

00:02:05.206 --> 00:02:10.085
And I loved her more than life itself.

00:02:10.086 --> 00:02:12.254
Rhaegar went south with Lyanna,

00:02:12.255 --> 00:02:15.090
hiding her away in Dome.

00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:19.886
What harm he inflicted on the poor girl,
the gods only know.

00:02:19.887 --> 00:02:24.433
Brandon Stark, Lyanna's eldest brother,
was outraged.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.686
He rode to King's Landing 
to confront the king

00:02:27.687 --> 00:02:31.607
and demand his sister's safe return.

00:02:31.608 --> 00:02:34.401
Instead, Aerys had him executed.

00:02:34.402 --> 00:02:38.322
His father, Rickard Stark, as well.

00:02:38.323 --> 00:02:42.534
There wasn't much left 
to discuss after that.

00:02:42.535 --> 00:02:47.039
Aerys feared their loved ones
would seek revenge for what he did.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.709
He was right to be afraid.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:55.005
Aerys wasted no time in calling 
for the heads of Brandon's younger brother,

00:02:55.006 --> 00:02:57.382
my friend Eddard Stark,

00:02:57.383 --> 00:03:00.385
and my head, too, of course.

00:03:00.386 --> 00:03:04.556
I'm sorry he didn't come 
looking for it himself.

00:03:04.557 --> 00:03:06.767
Alongside Jon Arryn of the Vale -

00:03:06.768 --> 00:03:09.519
the man who fostered 
Ned and I as children -

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.520
Baratheons, Starks and Tullys
all called their banners.

00:03:14.776 --> 00:03:17.235
Once our rebellion began,

00:03:17.236 --> 00:03:22.236
the Mad King's days were numbered.

